  "caption": "A Saturday birthday, then a very long Sunday run for Quinn.\n\nAlcohol can affect sleep, fluid balance and some recovery processes, though usually less dramatically than social media suggests; dose and timing matter most. Falling asleep faster after drinks is sedation, not better-quality sleep.\n\nWhat often helps: getting protein and fluid in after training first, finishing earlier to protect sleep, choosing low or zero-alcohol options, staying within the Australian guidelines of no more than 10 standard drinks a week and 4 on any day, and going easy in the days after an acute injury.\n\nAn injury that isn't improving after about two weeks, big swelling, locking or not being able to bear weight is worth assessing. Concerned about drinking? Chat with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
